From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:39:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] sensors: t31 sc4336p: sensor_set_vflip returns the real
 i2c result

sensor_set_vflip() started with ret = -1 and then added the results of the
read and the write, so a fully successful flip returned -1 and the ISP
driver logged "hvflip: sensor flip 0xN failed: -1" on every flip although
register 0x3221 was written. Return the read error, or the write result.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 common/sensor/t31/sc4336p.c | 11 +++++------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/sensor/t31/sc4336p.c b/common/sensor/t31/sc4336p.c
index 1dd1a642..f99087a3 100644
--- a/common/sensor/t31/sc4336p.c
+++ b/common/sensor/t31/sc4336p.c
@@ -801,19 +801,18 @@ static int sensor_g_chip_ident(struct tx_isp_subdev *sd, struct tx_isp_chip_iden
 }
 
 static int sensor_set_vflip(struct tx_isp_subdev *sd, int enable) {
-	int ret = -1;
+	int ret;
 	unsigned char val = 0x00;
 
-	ret += sensor_read(sd, 0x3221, &val);
+	ret = sensor_read(sd, 0x3221, &val);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 	if (enable & 0x02)
 		val |= 0x60;
 	else
 		val &= 0x9f;
-	ret += sensor_write(sd, 0x3221, val);
-	if (0 != ret)
-		return ret;
 
-	return 0;
+	return sensor_write(sd, 0x3221, val);
 }
 
 static int sensor_sensor_ops_ioctl(struct tx_isp_subdev *sd, unsigned int cmd, void *arg) {
